notes.text:
Retain complete nontrivially discretely valued K, smooth connected projective X/K in arbitrary dimension and ample L, with V=(L^n). P16.3 includes both equal characteristic (p,p) and mixed characteristic (0,p). The full requested result is not proved.

Established background on this actual axis: choose a continuous semipositive model reference ρ. Genuine model MA has raw mass V; BE Propositions 8.3/8.5 and Theorems 8.4/8.18 provide the continuous measure and model calculus. Ample L is semiample and its continuous psh metrics are psh-regularizable (Theorem 7.14), satisfying Theorem 8.4's hypothesis. These facts do not require characteristic-zero resolution.

For PL/model tests D_θ, with θ=c1(L,ρ), define Eθ(u)=((n+1)V)^{-1}Σ_j∫u(θ+dd^cu)^j∧θ^{n−j} and Jθ(ν)=sup_{D_θ}(Eθ(u)−∫u dν). The exact already established test-side raw condition is μ(Xan)=V and VJθ(μ/V)<∞. BJ-synth, arXiv:2307.01697v1, verifies the projective Berkovich data using intersection measures, integration by parts and the local Hodge index theorem. Its Section 1.3.2 does not identify HBC with N1 over every field; the positive cone is the preimage of the ample cone, which suffices here.

Example 2.20 establishes test-energy orthogonality using BE and the published relative-volume differentiability estimate. Definition 2.15 is a directed limit ∫(f−u)MAθ(u)→0 for tests u<f, not a prior assertion of continuous psh envelopes. Theorem 2.23 proves that maximizing test sequences have MAθ(u_j) converging strongly to ν. Theorem A completes the finite-energy measure space. The introduction expressly does not investigate potentials of finite energy. Hence these results neither produce a limiting usc psh potential nor identify the completed measures with E1/R. BJ-triv's equivalence between envelope regularity, potential completeness and surjectivity is proved in its trivial-valuation setting; it cannot be imported without the missing inputs.

A genuine but narrow nontrivial example exists in every dimension: if a smooth projective K°-model has irreducible special fiber and relatively ample extension of L, its reference metric has MAraw(0)=Vδξ. Concavity and the derivative at zero give Eθ(u)≤∫u dδξ, so Jθ(δξ)=0. This is an actual model solution for a particular target, not an arbitrary-measure existence theorem or construction of unbounded MA.

Gubler–Rabinoff 2506.13548v2 concerns classically psh functions and maximum principles; its introduction excludes MA construction from its subject. CLD 1204.6277v2 gives characteristic-independent local forms/currents and Bedford–Taylor theory without resolution, but no passage identifying all target global finite-energy metrics with its regularizable local class is proved here. Thuillier concerns curves; Berkovich 1993 supplies analytic/étale foundations. None is used to infer a higher-dimensional global equation theorem.

Remaining obligations for the full atom:
(1) construct the intended singular psh cone with monotone approximation and normalized compactness, replacing SNC/retraction/toroidal inputs;
(2) prove model positivity and envelope regularity or an adequate variational substitute without unproved resolution or extra function-field descent, including mixed characteristic;
(3) construct approximation-independent genuine mixed MA for unbounded E1 with positivity, integrability and full raw mass;
(4) prove equality of test and E1 dual suprema and the obstacle-energy derivative on that actual space;
(5) obtain an actual finite-energy maximizing psh potential for every correctly massed finite-dual-energy Radon measure of arbitrary support;
(6) prove unbounded locality/comparison and injectivity modulo constants.
Alterations, base change, normalization and universal homeomorphisms are not assumed to preserve these structures. Measure density is not substituted for item (5), and no restricted measure is renormalized.

